 tubulin-glutamic acid ligase activity. Involved in protein polyglutamylation. Predicted to be located in 9+0 non-motile cilium and ciliary basal body. Predicted to be active in cilium. [provided by Alliance of Genome Resources, Apr 2022]","ncbi_source":"NCBI Gene summary (RefSeq), via MyGene.info","uniprot_function":[{"accession":"Q6ZT98","text":"Polyglutamylase which modifies tubulin, generating polyglutamate side chains of variable lengths on the gamma-carboxyl group of specific glutamate residues within the C-terminal tail of tubulin (PubMed:16901895, PubMed:25959773). Mediates both ATP-dependent initiation and elongation steps of the polyglutamylation reaction (PubMed:16901895, PubMed:25959773). Preferentially modifies the beta-tubulin tail over an alpha-tail (PubMed:16901895, PubMed:25959773). Competes with monoglycylase TTLL3 for modification site on beta-tubulin substrate, thereby creating an anticorrelation between glycylation and glutamylation reactions (By similarity). Required for neurite growth; responsible for the strong increase in tubulin polyglutamylation during postnatal neuronal maturation (By similarity)."}],"uniprot_source":"UniProtKB/Swiss-Prot Function, release 2026_04","retrieved":"2026-10-21"}],"structures":[{"accession":"Q6ZT98","pdb_id":"4ylr","het_id":"ADP","resolution":2.55,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"ADP","ligand_class":"cofactor or substrate","ligand_note":null,"entry_title":"Tubulin Glutamylase","first_author":"Garnham, C.P.","n_authors":8,"journal":"Cell","year":2015,"doi":"10.1016/j.cell.2015.04.003","citation_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.cell.2015.04.003"},{"accession":"Q6ZT98","pdb_id":"4yls","het_id":"ANP","resolution":2.6,"method":"X-ray diffraction","ligand_rule":"heaviest non-additive 150-900 Da","datasets":["Mathys et al. 2019"],"ligand_name":"PHOSPHOAMINOPHOSPHONIC ACID-ADENYLATE ESTER","ligand_class":"cofactor or substrate"